WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.869
The choir leader came over to Rat.

2
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.877
"Can I help you, sir?" said the mouse.

3
00:00:21.878 --> 00:00:24.198
Rat spoke quietly.

4
00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:27.487
"Are the shops still open?" he asked.

5
00:00:27.488 --> 00:00:29.878
The mouse nodded politely.

6
00:00:29.879 --> 00:00:33.612
"Shops are open late this time of year," he said.

7
00:00:33.613 --> 00:00:37.666
Rat put some coins into the mouse's paw.

8
00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:40.041
"Great!" said Rat.

9
00:00:40.042 --> 00:00:44.878
"Go buy us some good food."

10
00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:48.748
The rest of the mice sat down by the fire.

11
00:00:48.749 --> 00:00:52.202
Mole was opening his empty cupboards.

12
00:00:52.203 --> 00:00:56.352
"Oh dear," Mole said, shaking his head.

13
00:00:56.353 --> 00:01:01.271
"Now," cried Rat, "what shall we do for fun?"

14
00:01:01.272 --> 00:01:04.678
Mole turned and looked at Rat.

15
00:01:04.679 --> 00:01:09.819
"Well," said Mole, "these mice are actors too.

16
00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.136
They did a play about pirates last year."

17
00:01:13.137 --> 00:01:17.868
"Really? Let's see!" cried Rat.

18
00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:21.209
The mice whispered together.

19
00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:24.809
"Samuel should do it," said one, pointing.

20
00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:28.538
"Yes, Sammy will do it!" said the others.

21
00:01:28.539 --> 00:01:32.544
One young mouse stood shyly.

22
00:01:32.545 --> 00:01:35.636
"Say something from the play," said Rat.

23
00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:38.134
"Ahem," said Samuel.

24
00:01:38.135 --> 00:01:40.798
"Go on," said Mole.

25
00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:43.943
"Don't be shy," said Rat.

26
00:01:43.944 --> 00:01:49.078
"Um, um . . . ," Samuel said.

27
00:01:49.079 --> 00:01:51.866
The other mice encouraged him.

28
00:01:51.867 --> 00:01:55.201
"You can do it, Sammy!" they said.

29
00:01:55.202 --> 00:02:00.546
"Um, um," the young mouse repeated.

30
00:02:00.547 --> 00:02:03.740
"Here now, little one," said Rat.

31
00:02:03.741 --> 00:02:05.876
"Everyone is waiting."

32
00:02:05.877 --> 00:02:10.210
"Oh Rat," said Mole, "give him a chance."

33
00:02:10.211 --> 00:02:14.930
Suddenly the door flew open.
